    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29110" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Minaei</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Minnaei</span></b> ), ōrum, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of
				Arabia, celebrated for their myrrh and frankincense</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 28,
				32, § 155</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Prisc.
				Perieg. 888</span></i>.—Hence, adj.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĭnae-us</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
				the Minæi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 14, 30, § 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 16, 35, § 69</span></i>
			.</div>
